<task id="032" project="spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Governed narrow-allow-list preference-producer → pre-turn tool hint (FR-09)</title>
    <phase>3 — E3 feedback→memory loop</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <!-- COMPLETED 2026-08-17 (opus/xhigh, FULL — the injection-defense boundary). Design: the ONE sanctioned seam where a
         LEARNED preference biases behavior, bounded to be injection-safe. NEW static PreferenceDirectiveProducer
         (Services/Ai/Context/, pure function mirroring StatedProfileRenderer): a CLOSED allow-list of named directives
         (task-agenda-default, daily-briefing-default) is matched by DETERMINISTIC ordinal marker-containment (no LLM, no
         classifier) against the caller's CONFIRMED Preference facts; a match emits a FIXED SERVER-AUTHORED hint that biases
         the DEFAULT of an ALREADY-AVAILABLE capability. Wired as a 4th sibling userFragment producer on ContextBinder
         (ResolvePreferenceDirectiveFragmentAsync, reads IMemoryItemStore.GetForUserAsync, soft-fails to null). THE BOUNDS:
         (1) PROMPT-ONLY — the hint folds into the userFragment; it NEVER touches AgentToolFilterContext (the mount set stays
         preference-blind; proven — the two structural-invariant tests stay at 7 members, NO 032 member added → a preference
         reaches the grounding filter through NO member at all). Never grants a capability. (2) Never alters a fact (adds no
         grounded data; the hint re-states "every fact must come from a tool result"). (3) INJECTION-SAFE — the user's RAW
         preference text is NEVER emitted as an instruction; only the closed-set match fires the fixed hint (poisoned-text test
         proves an injection payload in the preference emits only the server hint). (4) CONFIRMED-ONLY — an unconfirmed
         ai-derived inference (task-031 dormant candidate) never steers (ADR-042 coherence). (5) Off-allow-list directive =
         inert. (6) guillemet DATA-guard discipline preserved (DirectiveGuard line states the hard bound). trustLevel inert
         (#616). Also FIXED a pre-existing task-011 regression: 2 invariant tests (ContextBinderOrgContextTests +
         StatedProfileSecurityTests) hardcoded AgentToolFilterContext=6 props; 011 added AdvisoryToolAllowList (→7) without
         updating them — reconciled + repurposed as live 032 guards. 8 producer bounds tests + 2 fixed = 85/85 ContextBinder
         suite green; build 0 err; publish 43.68 MB compressed (≤60, Δ≈0); CVE clean. Step 9.5 CLEAN (adr-check ADR-039
         preference-only / ADR-042 / ADR-013 / §10 / §11, 0 violations; code-review 0 blocking — 1 note: independent
         GetForUserAsync read, acceptable). Escalation trigger did NOT fire. 033 adds the eval + wider bounds coverage. -->
    <!-- ORIGINAL: <status>pending</status> -->

    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Crosses the advisory→bounded-directive line at the injection-defense boundary; a preference-producer seam on ContextBinder that must never become a capability grant.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>THE injection-defense boundary — a preference may hint/trigger an allow-listed grounded capability but must NEVER grant a capability or alter a fact; highest E3 sensitivity.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>Wave3-E3</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits ContextBinder / a new producer seam (BFF, ADR-039 preference-only boundary) — coordinate BFF PRs via /conflict-check; depends on 030 (the Preference fact type).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>030</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ai</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Implement a governed preference-producer seam: a CLOSED allow-list of named standing directives (e.g. "always summarize my tasks", "always open my briefing") maps ONLY to pre-turn tool HINTS. A preference may bias/trigger an allow-listed grounded capability (e.g. bias the FR-01 task-agenda capability's default), but MUST NEVER grant a capability or alter a fact. Preserve the injection-defense discipline: the stated profile MUST NOT feed `AgentToolFilterContext` except through this ONE sanctioned bounded hint (ADR-039 preference-only), and the `StatedProfileRenderer` guillemet «...» DATA-guard is preserved. An off-allow-list directive has NO tool-selection effect. Keep `trustLevel` inert (ADR-042 #616).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. .NET 8 Minimal API + AI-governance expertise; deeply comfortable with ADR-039's grounded-execution / preference-only rule, prompt-injection defense (the guillemet DATA-guard), and the `AgentToolFilterContext` / pre-filter boundary.</role>
  <goal>A CLOSED allow-list of named standing directives maps ONLY to pre-turn tool HINTS: "always summarize my tasks" biases the FR-01 capability's default behavior; a preference never grants a capability or alters a fact; the injection-defense guard (guillemet DATA-guard, ADR-039 preference-only) is preserved; off-allow-list directives are inert.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-09 — the governed steering step, the highest-sensitivity E3 change. Today `StatedProfileReader.cs` is ADVISORY-ONLY (its header lines 22–23 + the `ContextBinder` ctor doc lines 116–117 state it MUST NOT touch `AgentToolFilterContext`) and `StatedProfileRenderer.cs`'s FreeTextGuard wraps stated text in guillemets «...» as a DATA-guard against injection. This task adds a NEW bounded seam that deliberately crosses the advisory line — but only within tight bounds: a CLOSED allow-list of named directives ("always summarize my tasks", "always open my briefing") produces a pre-turn tool HINT that biases the default behavior of an allow-listed grounded capability (the FR-01 task-agenda capability). Crossing the line is bounded by design: a preference may bias/trigger an allow-listed capability, but NEVER grant a capability nor alter a fact. The stated profile still MUST NOT feed `AgentToolFilterContext` EXCEPT through this one sanctioned bounded hint (ADR-039 preference-only). The guillemet DATA-guard is preserved; off-allow-list directives have no tool-selection effect. ADR-042's deferred hard-governance stays deferred to #616 (`trustLevel` inert). The producer consumes the `Preference` items from tasks 030/031; recall/userFragment assembly is in `ContextBinder.ResolveUserFragmentAsync` (~:553–583).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Context/ContextBinder.cs (userFragment assembly ~:553–583; ctor doc lines 116–117 — stated profile MUST NOT touch AgentToolFilterContext; the new producer seam attaches here)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Context/StatedProfileReader.cs (advisory-only; header lines 22–23 — MUST NOT touch AgentToolFilterContext)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Context/StatedProfileRenderer.cs (FreeTextGuard — guillemet «...» DATA-guard, preserve)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Memory/MemoryFactType.cs (`Preference` — from task 030; the producer's input)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/AgentToolCatalogProjector.cs + AgentToolProjection.cs PreFilter (the pre-turn hint targets an allow-listed grounded capability here)</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (add/update unit tests for the bounds — NFR-08)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039" scope="the producer">Allow-listed named directives ONLY → a pre-turn tool HINT; the stated profile MUST NOT feed `AgentToolFilterContext` EXCEPT through this ONE sanctioned bounded hint; the guillemet «...» DATA-guard (advisory injection-defense) is preserved.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-042" scope="preferences">`trustLevel` carried INERT (deferred hard-governance owned by #616) — do NOT implement untrusted-origin ban / trustLevel enforcement / memory-poisoning evals.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="the allow-list">CLOSED set of named directives — an OFF-allow-list directive has NO tool-selection effect; MUST NOT accept free-text preference steering (owner Q2: narrow allow-list only).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="the hint's power">A preference may bias/trigger an allow-listed grounded capability but MUST NEVER grant a capability nor alter a fact — the bound is the point of the task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="BFF §10" scope="every BFF-touching change">Publish size ≤60 MB compressed (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs) — measure and report absolute + delta; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08" scope="the producer">Add/update unit tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ that exercise the bounds.</constraint>
  </constraints>
