  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Define the closed allow-list shape: named directives (e.g. "always summarize my tasks", "always open my briefing") → a hint targeting an allow-listed grounded capability (the FR-01 task-agenda capability). No free text.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement the producer as a PRE-TURN HINT that biases the allow-listed capability's DEFAULT behavior — attached at the sanctioned seam on `ContextBinder`; it does NOT grant a capability or alter any fact.</step>
    <step order="3">Preserve the guillemet «...» DATA-guard in `StatedProfileRenderer`; keep `StatedProfileReader` advisory-only (it MUST NOT touch `AgentToolFilterContext` except via this one sanctioned hint).</step>
    <step order="4">Ensure off-allow-list directives are INERT — no tool-selection effect.</step>
    <step order="5">Keep `trustLevel` inert (ADR-042 #616).</step>
    <step order="6">Add/extend unit tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ for the bounds (biases default; off-allow-list inert; never grants a capability; never alters a fact; DATA-guard preserved).</step>
    <step order="7">dotnet build + dotnet publish size check; record absolute size + delta; run the vulnerable-package scan.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a requested directive cannot be expressed as an allow-listed pre-turn HINT without letting the preference grant a capability or change a fact, STOP and escalate (ADR-039 / ADR-042 boundary) rather than widening the allow-list to free text.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>`StatedProfileReader` is advisory-only and never steers tool selection; no seam turns a standing directive into a bounded pre-turn hint.</existing>
    <extension>NO — a NEW bounded seam (steering crosses the advisory line by design, but bounded to a closed allow-list → hints only). Existing readers stay advisory.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>"always summarize my tasks" can never act automatically — the P3 loop stays open even after the preference is persisted (tasks 030/031).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">the governed preference-producer seam (Services/Ai/Context — closed allow-list → pre-turn hint)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ preference-producer bounds unit tests</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">"always summarize my tasks" biases the FR-01 capability's default behavior (via a pre-turn tool hint).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An off-allow-list directive has NO tool-selection effect (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A preference NEVER grants a capability nor alters a fact (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The injection-defense guard is preserved — the guillemet «...» DATA-guard holds; the stated profile feeds `AgentToolFilterContext` ONLY through the sanctioned bounded hint.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The bounds are unit-tested in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ and pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size ≤60 MB reported (absolute + delta); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Code-trace anchors: StatedProfileReader header lines 22–23 + ContextBinder ctor doc 116–117 (advisory-only, MUST NOT touch AgentToolFilterContext); StatedProfileRenderer FreeTextGuard (guillemet DATA-guard); ContextBinder ResolveUserFragmentAsync ~:553–583. Depends on 030 (Preference fact type); consumes preferences persisted by 031. The bounds this task enforces are the exact target of task 033's bounds tests. Run /conflict-check before the BFF PR — the injection-defense boundary is the highest-sensitivity E3 change.</notes>
